 "title": "Your app crashes at 3 AM",
 "sources": [
  "Kubernetes docs, Pod Lifecycle (https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/pods/pod-lifecycle/, fetched 2026-11-24): restartPolicy 'The default value is Always'; 'After containers in a Pod exit, the kubelet restarts them with an exponential backoff delay (10s, 20s, 40s, …), that is capped at 300 seconds (5 minutes)'; CrashLoopBackOff 'indicates that the backoff delay mechanism is currently in effect for a given container that is in a crash loop'; liveness probes 'could catch a deadlock, where an application is running, but unable to make progress'; 'If a container fails its liveness probe more times than the configured tolerance, the kubelet restarts that container'.",
  "Kubernetes docs, Components (https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/components/, fetched 2026-11-24): node components 'Run on every node'; kubelet 'Ensures that Pods are running, including their containers'."
 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Your app crashes at three in the morning. Who restarts it before anyone wakes up? Guess.",
   "caps": "CRASH AT *3 AM | WHO *RESTARTS IT? | *GUESS"
  },
  {
   "text": "In Kubernetes, an agent on every machine, the kubelet, keeps your containers running.",
   "caps": "THE *KUBELET | ON EVERY *MACHINE | KEEPS IT *RUNNING"
  },
  {
   "text": "A pod's restart policy defaults to always, so when a container exits, it's started again.",
   "caps": "RESTART: *ALWAYS | EXITS? *STARTED AGAIN"
  },
  {
   "text": "And a liveness probe catches an app that's running but stuck, and restarts it too.",
   "caps": "*LIVENESS PROBE | RUNNING BUT *STUCK | *RESTARTED"
  },
  {
   "text": "So the answer is nobody. The kubelet does it.",
   "caps": "ANSWER: *NOBODY | THE *KUBELET"
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's the catch: a restart doesn't fix a bug. Crash again, and it waits ten seconds, then twenty, then forty.",
   "caps": "THE *CATCH | NOT A *FIX | 10, 20, *40 SECONDS"
  },
  {
   "text": "Capped at five minutes. That's the CrashLoopBackOff you see in kubectl.",
   "caps": "*5 MINUTE CAP | *CRASHLOOPBACKOFF"
  },
  {
   "text": "So restarts buy you time, not a fix. Did you guess right?",
   "caps": "BUYS *TIME | NOT A *FIX | DID YOU GUESS *RIGHT?"
  }
 ],
